.TH LIFEBOAT.CONF 5 "2026-11-07" "lifeboat 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
lifeboat.conf \- Lifeboat configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/lifeboat/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
A TOML file with three sections:
.BR [settings] ,
.B [destinations.NAME]
tables and
.B [jobs.NAME]
tables. Names use lowercase letters, digits, "\-" and "_" (up to 32).
Edit it with
.B sudo lifeboat config edit
(validates before saving) or the Lifeboat app. Unknown keys are errors, so typos are caught.
Values not given take the defaults shown.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.BR hostname " = """""
Folder name for this PC inside destinations. Empty means the system host name.
.TP
.BR notify_on " = ""failure"""
.BR always ,
.B failure
(failures and warnings; skipped runs only once no backup succeeded for 7 days) or
.BR never .
.TP
.BR notify_desktop " = true"
Pop-up notifications for logged-in users.
.TP
.BR ntfy_url " = """""
An ntfy topic URL. An access token, if needed, goes in
.I /etc/lifeboat/secrets.toml
as
.BR ntfy_token .
.TP
.BR log_keep " = 30"
Logs kept per job.
.SH DESTINATIONS
.TP
.BR type " = ""folder"" | ""drive"" | ""nfs"""
.TP
.BR path " (folder)"
An existing absolute path, normally on a second drive. A folder on the system's own disk is
refused unless
.BR same_disk_ok " = true."
.TP
.BR uuid " (drive)"
Filesystem UUID (see
.BR "lifeboat drives" ).
For a LUKS drive use the LUKS container's UUID; it's unlocked with
.B keyfile
if not already open. The drive is mounted under
.I /run/lifeboat/mnt
when needed and unmounted afterwards. Not connected means the run is skipped, not failed.
.TP
.BR server ", " export ", " options " (nfs)"
Lifeboat mounts the share itself with
.B soft,timeo=150,retrans=3
so a dead NAS fails the run instead of freezing the PC.
.B options
adds mount options such as
.BR vers=4.2 .
.TP
.BR subdir " (drive, nfs)"
Use a folder inside the drive or share.
.TP
.BR encrypted " = false"
Set when the storage is encrypted (detected automatically for LUKS drives and folders on
dm-crypt). Required for the
.B secrets
module and LUKS header backups.
.SH JOBS
.TP
.B destination
Name of a destination.
.TP
.BR enabled " = true"
When false, only manual runs happen.
.TP
.BR modules " = []"
Any of:
.BR etc ,
.BR packages ,
.BR disk\-layout ,
.BR services ,
.BR dotfiles ,
.BR configs ,
.BR desktop ,
.BR home ,
.BR browsers ,
.BR secrets ,
.BR system .
.B lifeboat modules
describes them.
.TP
.BR users " = []"
Users whose home folders the per-user modules cover. Empty means every regular user.
.TP
.BR include " = []"
Extra absolute paths to back up.
.TP
.BR exclude " = []"
rsync exclude patterns, for example
.B "/home/*/Videos"
or
.BR "*.iso" .
.TP
.BR one_file_system " = true"
Don't descend into other filesystems mounted inside backed-up folders.
.TP
.BR allow_unencrypted_secrets " = false"
Save keys and LUKS headers even on unencrypted destinations.
.TP
.BR allow_lossy " = false"
Allow destinations that can't keep file owners at all.
.TP
.BR pre_command ", " post_command " = """""
Shell commands run as root before and after the backup. A failing
.B pre_command
fails the run.
.B post_command
gets
.BR LIFEBOAT_STATUS " and " LIFEBOAT_SNAPSHOT .
.TP
.BR healthcheck_url " = """""
Pinged healthchecks.io style:
.IR url/start ,
.IR url ,
.IR url/fail .
.SS [jobs.NAME.schedule]
.TP
.BR mode " = ""manual"""
.BR manual ,
.BR hourly ,
.BR daily ,
.BR weekly ,
.BR monthly ,
.BR custom .
.TP
.BR time " = ""02:30"""
24-hour time. Hourly uses only the minutes.
.TP
.BR weekday " = ""sun"""
.TP
.BR day " = 1"
Day of the month, 1 to 28.
.TP
.BR calendar " = """""
For
.BR custom :
a
.BR systemd.time (7)
calendar expression such as
.BR "Mon..Fri 18:00" .
.TP
.BR random_delay_min " = 0"
.PP
Missed runs (PC off) run at the next boot.
.SS [jobs.NAME.triggers]
.TP
.BR before_pacman " = false"
Run before every pacman transaction. Repeated transactions within 10 minutes reuse the last backup.
.TP
.BR on_drive_connect " = false"
Run when the destination drive is plugged in (drive destinations only).
.TP
.BR min_interval_hours " = 0"
Skip these extra runs if the last success is newer than this.
.SS [jobs.NAME.retention]
.TP
.BR keep_last " = 3, " keep_hourly " = 0, " keep_daily " = 7, " keep_weekly " = 4, " keep_monthly " = 6, " keep_yearly " = 0"
Keep the newest N snapshots, then the newest snapshot in each of the last N hours, days,
ISO weeks, months and years. A snapshot kept by any rule stays.
.TP
.BR keep_within_days " = 0"
Keep everything from the last N days.
.TP
.BR keep_all " = false"
Never remove snapshots.
.TP
.BR min_free_gb " = 0"
After normal pruning, remove the oldest snapshots until this much space is free.
.TP
.BR prune_after_backup " = true"
.PP
Pinned snapshots and the newest snapshot are never removed.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
[settings]
notify_on = "failure"

[destinations.usb]
type = "drive"
uuid = "3f2a9c1e-5b7d-4e2a-9c1e-5b7d4e2a9c1e"

[destinations.nas]
type = "nfs"
server = "192.168.20.50"
export = "/mnt/MainPool/Backups"
subdir = "pcs"

[jobs.system]
destination = "usb"
modules = ["etc", "packages", "disk\-layout", "services", "dotfiles", "configs", "desktop"]
[jobs.system.schedule]
mode = "daily"
time = "12:30"
[jobs.system.triggers]
before_pacman = true

[jobs.home]
destination = "nas"
modules = ["home", "browsers"]
exclude = ["/home/*/Downloads"]
[jobs.home.schedule]
mode = "weekly"
weekday = "sun"
time = "03:00"
[jobs.home.retention]
keep_last = 2
keep_weekly = 8
keep_monthly = 12
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lifeboat (8),
.BR systemd.time (7)
